id=ternak_tt
name=Ternak TT — Zygisk Fresh Persona
version=v1.1.7
versionCode=1107
author=Ilham311
description=Zygisk device spoofer targeting TikTok (musically/trill/lite) + Grab Passenger. 6-layer Java hook + 78 native prop spoofs + L7 TYPED spoof tables + companion fork+setns bind mount overlay. v1.0.15: target list moved out of the binary into /data/adb/modules/ternak_tt/target.txt — hot-reloaded by companion (mtime watch), so add/remove TikTok clones or Grab Driver without rebuilding. Wire protocol: Zygisk .so sends pkg name to companion, companion rejects non-targets with len=0. CLI gains `ternak-tt targets`. L7 SPI/SPL/SPB gain SUPPRESS label for known-noise keys. Auto-summarizer on Action tap breaks SPOOF hits out by hook layer (L1/L2/L7-SPB/SPI/SPL). v1.1.6: Path B rearchitected — lsplant consumed as prebuilt .so from lsplant-standalone AAR on Maven Central; liblsplant.so shipped via $MODPATH/system/lib{,64}/ overlay so DT_NEEDED resolves inside app processes. v1.1.7: swapped jmpews/Dobby → bytedance/android-inline-hook (ShadowHook) because Dobby master stopped compiling on NDK r26d (ADRP relocation, RuntimeModule::load_address rename, missing core/arch/Cpu.h). ShadowHook is actively maintained, has the same lsplant call surface (hook_func_addr + unhook), and ships as libternak_shadowhook.so via /system/lib{,64}/ (renamed SONAME to avoid collision with TikTok's own libshadowhook.so). Also fixed CI helper dex compile: javac now runs with -bootclasspath android.jar (workflow installs platforms;android-34). riscv64 AAR variant no longer copied. Works on Zygisk-Next / HMA-OSS.
updateJson=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Ilham311/Tt/main/update.json
